/* THE CLOCK ROW — Info tab. A camera whose clock is wrong puts events at the wrong minute,
   searches the archive for the wrong day and leaves bookmarks pointing at nothing, and every
   one of those reads as a bug in Vigil until you can see the clock. "zone corrected" marks a
   firmware that labels local time as UTC: the skew shown IS the zone offset and the camera's
   clock is in fact correct, so without this the user would go and reset a clock that is fine. */
"Clock" = "Clock";
"zone corrected" = "zone corrected";

